  "what_it_is": {
    "prose": "HSL is India's oldest shipyard (founded 1941) and is now a Miniratna Category-I defence PSU specialising in submarine refits, DSRV-mothership construction, naval shipbuilding and repair. HSL completed the fastest-ever normal refit of an EKM-class (Kilo) submarine on 21 Jul 2025 — INS Sindhukirti refit (Mar 2023 MoD contract) including modification and testing of escape hatches for the Deep Submergence Rescue Vehicle. HSL built and delivered INS Nistar (first DSV, Jul 19, 2025) and INS Nipun (second DSV, Jul 30, 2026) — the DSVs serve as mother ships for the Indian Navy's DSRV deep-submergence rescue system. HSL is in talks with the Vietnam People's Navy for Kilo-class submarine refits (Aug 2025).",
    "sources": [
      "src-01",
      "src-02",
      "src-03",
      "src-04",
      "src-05"
    ]
  },
